From: SaaiOS <os@saaios>
Subject: synaptics td4150: since26 hold IRQ, first 0x45 drain, no LCD reset

since25 first 0x45 still waited 3s (drain only on retry). Retry drain
n=0 gpio=0 because IRQ owned the line, then skip-wait never sent 0x45.
Pulse used gpio_lcd_rst (panel, not TSP). Reading 0x1b plen=2 does not
drop ATTN; cap-8 drain cannot catch up; level IRQ storms ~10k/s.

since26:
- First 0x45: disable_irq (nosync from threaded ISR), force one
  header+payload read of leftover ATTN, log once, chunked 0x45, then
  enable_irq. If drain n=0 and gpio still 0, do not skip 0x45.
- Never pulse gpio_lcd_rst. reset-gpio=-1 logs "no TSP reset".
- First need_*=0 0x1b in RomBoot: idle flag + disable_irq until 0x45
  finishes. Silent consume only. No printk per IRQ. No do_polling.
- Keep: PAGE_SIZE 16-aligned 0x45 chunks, 0x30 only if need_*, skip-0x30
  once, no ENABLE_REPORT 0x05, no IRQ unwind on timeout.
- 0x45 success: IDENTIFY 0x02 = firmware started. Fail: romboot_ok=0,
  IRQ stays registered, in_hdl_mode stock (RomBoot 0x04).

Applies after syna-tcm-romboot-drain-attn.patch.

